  "question": {
    "text": "The total number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-digit numbers whose greatest common divisor with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;is _____."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1000",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> be the four digit number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> is an odd integer which is divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> but not by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> digit odd multiples of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1005</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1011</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>9999</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>1500</mn></math></p><p>digit odd multiples of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1017</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1035</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>9999</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>500</mn></math></p><p>Hence number of such <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1500</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></math></p>"
  }
}